    "updated_at": "2025-11-13T01:45:57Z",
    "body": "@annevk @DCtheTall Please forgive my poor English.\r\n\r\nafter 3 month, the fix is no merge to chrome?\r\n\r\nhttps://issues.chromium.org/issues/458852787\r\n\r\nWe indeed need to be quite careful about modifying this, but this is clearly not compliant with the specification. For Chrome it is a legacy issue, and given Chrome’s market share it is quite feasible for application developers to find workarounds for the problem.\r\n\r\nIn the end I believe this fix can be merged directly:\r\n1. Chrome itself handles Set-Cookie correctly, meaning this issue only affects the browser API operations on cookies.\r\n2. keep `path: /test`, not added trailingSlash `path: /test/` will have no impact on existing systems — according to the specification, as long as the path is `/test` or `/test/**`, the cookie should be accessible, so the change simply adds support for `/test`.\r\n\r\nhttps://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6265#section-5.1.4",
    "author_association": "NONE",
